DISTRIBUTION MODEL:

Patchy uses a source-open, binary-paid model:

  - Source code is free under GPL v3. You are welcome to compile Patchy
    yourself at no cost.

  - Official pre-built binaries are available for a small fee, which supports
    ongoing development.

This model is inspired by projects such as Kushview Element and is fully
compliant with the GPL v3 license terms.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOTE ON JUCE:

Patchy is built using the JUCE framework (https://juce.com), which is
licensed under the GNU General Public License v3. Patchy is distributed
under the same GPL v3 terms — source code and pre-built binaries alike.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOTE ON PAX:

The Pax API (Pax/PaxAPI.h) is separately licensed under the MIT
License (see Pax/LICENSE). Pax developers are free to license their
own Pax code under any terms they choose, including proprietary licenses.
Pax are considered separate works communicating with Patchy at arm's
length via the Pax API.
